# ── CPU stuck at 700MHz: clk-qoriq's create_one_cmux() trusts whatever
#    clksel the core mux register is set to at Linux probe time as the
#    "rated maximum" and filters out everything faster. NXP's stock
#    U-Boot pre-selects the fast PLL1 tap before booting Linux; this
#    project's U-Boot doesn't, so Linux inherits the reset-default slow
#    tap (PLL2/div2, 700MHz) and permanently excludes the faster,
#    already-locked-and-running PLL1 taps (confirmed identical RCW +
#    identical live clk tree vs a board that boots at 1.6GHz). Fixes
#    cpuinfo_max_freq 700MHz -> 1600MHz. Scoped to ls1046a-clockgen only. ──
# Upstream-Status: Inappropriate | Risk-Tier: C
4010-clk-qoriq-ls1046a-cmux-full-range.patch

